Implement user story SKY-002-b: Vitest tests for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch (no real network calls). Tests must cover: RapidAPI URL and header construction, successful response parsing, HTTP error rejection, missing/empty API key constructor errors, malformed response parse errors, and mock mode behavior (MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns fixture without fetch; other values perform real fetch).

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach fetch restoration — no real network calls in any test
- Test verifies correct RapidAPI URL construction and that the apiKey is included in request headers
- Test verifies a successful API response is correctly parsed into FlightResult[] matching the interface shape
- Test verifies HTTP 4xx/5xx responses cause searchFlights to reject with an Error containing the status code
- Test verifies missing API key (omitted and empty-string cases) causes constructor to throw an Error referencing the missing key
- Test verifies malformed or missing-fields response body causes searchFlights to reject with a descriptive parse/validation Error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture data and global fetch is never invoked; test verifies other values ('false', empty, unset) result in a real fetch call
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient class is exported from './skyscanner/client' (relative path from test file location)
- constructor signature: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string })
- constructor throws Error with exact message: 'API key is required. Provide it via constructor or RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' when apiKey is undefined, null, or empty string
- constructor reads RAPIDAPI_KEY from process.env when apiKey parameter is not provided
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- searchFlights checks process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict string comparison, case-sensitive)
- when MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true', searchFlights returns deterministic fixture data from #getMockResults() without calling fetch
- fixture data contains 3 flights: prices 299, 199, 399 USD with airlines MockAir, BudgetFly, PremiumAir
- when MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API is 'false', empty string, or unset, searchFlights makes real fetch call
- URL construction: https://skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com/v3/flights/search?origin=<>&destination=<>&date=<>&adults=<>
- query param names: origin, destination, date, adults (adults only appended if defined)
- fetch headers: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' with apiKey value, 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com'
- fetch method: GET
- on non-ok response: throws Error with message 'HTTP error: ${response.status}'
- #parseFlightResults validates response is object, has results array, and each result has all 7 required fields with correct types
- parse errors throw Error with messages starting with 'Invalid response: ' followed by specific issue
- no validation on SearchParams fields (origin, destination, date can be any string, adults any number including 0 or negative)
- no retry logic on failed requests
- no timeout handling on fetch calls

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
vi.mock('<import-path-to-SkyscannerClient>', () => ({
  SkyscannerClient: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined),
  })),
}));
```

